ice: Case Study Insights**";s:4:"type";s:2:"ul";s:5:"level";i:2;}i:10;a:4:{s:3:"hid";s:10:"conclusion";s:5:"title";s:14:"**Conclusion**";s:4:"type";s:2:"ul";s:5:"level";i:2;}}s:8:"abstract";s:437:"EXPRESSION OF INTEREST

The Expression of Interest (EOI) serves as the foundational step in India’s insolvency resolution framework, ensuring structured participation from credible investors while safeguarding the interests of creditors and stakeholders. Governed by Regulation 36A of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Board of India (CIRP) Regulations, 2016, the EOI process establishes eligibility, transparency, and competitive bidding.";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1746424412;s:8:"modified";i:1746427051;}s:7:"creator";s:4:"Name";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1746427051;s:2:"ip";s:12:"49.43.99.166";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:59:"investors:investment_teasers:teasers:expression_of_interest";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:-96;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:4:"Name";}}}